# ─── 4. DATA — runtime state, not source ─────────────────────────────────
# The canonical runtime root is `data/`. Two things under it are tracked
# source and have to stay reachable: the investigation-queue marker and the
# store test fixtures. Everything else in there is runtime.
# `!/data/` comes first: `/data/*` alone would keep excluding the directory
# itself, and a directory git excludes is one it never descends into. The
# leading slash matters: without it the rule also matched `src/ikigai/data/`.
!/data/
/data/*
!/data/investigation_queue/
/data/investigation_queue/*
!/data/investigation_queue/.keep
!/data/test-fixtures/
/data/*.db
/data/*.json
/data/*.jsonl
/data/chroma_db/
/data/*.log
/data/session-*.md
/data/*-sessions/
/data/pytest-tmp/
# The store layer is PUBLISHED (ADR-037 D4): the pool and the repository are
# the only code that talks to the driver. `/src/data/` excluded the whole
# DIRECTORY, and that also killed the negations under it — git never
# descends into a directory it excluded, so a file re-included beneath an
# excluded parent stays invisible. The directory is left alone here; only its
# junk is ignored, and the four real files are named back.
/src/data/*
!/src/data/__init__.py
!/src/data/AGENTS.md
!/src/data/client.py
!/src/data/repository.py
/src/data/ikigai_checkpoints.db
/src/ikigai/data/
/src/ikigai/vault/
/tests/data/pytest-tmp/
/vibe-ops/**/*.db
/vibe-ops/chroma_db/

# ─── 5. VAULT — prose is source, runtime artifacts are not ───────────────
# The source vault (wikilinks, markdown) IS tracked. Runtime artifacts
# inside it are ignored.
vault/.venv/
vault/__pycache__/
vault/.ruff_cache/
vault/.mypy_cache/
vault/.pytest_cache/
vault/.db
/vault/.vault_events.jsonl
/vault/ikigai/decisions/*.jsonl

# ─── 6. BUILD ARTIFACTS AND VENDORED THIRD-PARTY ────────────────────────
# First-party Go tool at src/operational/medic/ (module github.com/life-oss/medic).
# 2026-08-28 audit: 24 MB of committed .exe was inflating every clone.
# Source (.go, go.mod, go.sum) IS tracked; binaries are local build outputs.
/src/operational/medic/medic.exe
/src/operational/medic/bin/
/archive/legacy-pav/src-operational/medic/medic.exe
/archive/legacy-pav/src-operational/medic/bin/
# M41 planning-with-files submodule unlink: the directory is a
# self-contained third-party fork with its own .git/; we don't track it in
# the parent repo.
/strategics/planning-with-files/
# BYD D2 Plotly HTMLs (regenerable artifacts) — 6 HTMLs at ~4.85 MB each.
/src/ikigai/data/matheus/**/outputs/*.html

# ─── 7. SCOPE — the pre-ADR-037 system (ADR-037, 2026-11-02) ─────────────
# The remote branch carries the canonical, multi-device, prod-deployable code
# only: the DOM (`src/contracts/`), the store client (`src/data/`), the
# service layer (`src/services/`), the transport (`src/transport/`), the
# vault prose, the specs and the tests of those.
#
# The pre-ADR-037 runtime is UNPUBLISHED, not deleted: the files stay on the
# owner's disk and in the git history; they are simply not on the branch.
# The first execution of ADR-037 ignored individual FILES inside trees that
# stayed published — so 84 of the 91 files in `sys_ikigai/` and 25 of the 26
# in `src/mesh/` kept shipping. The trees are now unpublished as units.
/sys_ikigai/
/src/mesh/
/interfaces/
/vibe-ops/
/src/agents/
/src/tuiboard/
/src/solverforge_calendar/
/src/ikigai/src/agents/
/src/ikigai/src/chat/
/src/ikigai/src/mcp_server/
/src/ikigai/src/plugins/
/src/ikigai/src/observability/
/src/ikigai/src/ikigai_wrapper.py
/src/ikigai/src/gateway_client.py
/src/ikigai/bin/
/src/ikigai/MCP_GATEWAY.md
/src/ikigai/ikigai.bat
/src/ikigai/start_mcp_gateway.sh
/plugins/paperclipai/
/langgraph.json
# The retired root project. Its manifest declared `packages = ["life", ...]`
# — a package that does not exist in this repository — and a console script
# pointing at `src.mesh.taskdog_cli`, the fork mesh that leaves the branch
# above. The canonical package is `src/ikigai/pyproject.toml`; the service
# ships as source with an explicit PYTHONPATH (see deploy/Dockerfile).
/pyproject.toml
/uv.lock
/constraints.txt
# The root-level suite of the retired runtime: it imported `sys_ikigai` and
# `src.mesh` directly. The canonical suite is `src/ikigai/tests/`.
/tests/
# The PC-only operational tooling: the loop daemons, the paperclip spawner,
# the taskdog shims and the fork smoke scripts. They drive the retired
# runtime, and a branch that publishes the data layer has no use for them.
/scripts/
/bin/
# The archived PAV kernel (ADR-013). ADR-037 §"publicação independente" is
# the clause that says the archive stays on the owner's disk and out of the
# branch.
/archive/
# The algorithm docset — 27 documents on the PAV / Q_HE / hysteresis-FSM
# axiomatic stack. ADR-037 D1 defers the algorithms to LAST: they need real
# data to be worth anything, and the kernel they describe is archived. The
# documents stay on the owner's disk; they do not ship.
/docs/auto-performance-os/

# The retired test suite: every top-level module under src/ikigai/tests/
# tests the retired runtime, except the four that survive and are named
# explicitly. One rule for the class, four for the exceptions.
/src/ikigai/tests/*.py
!/src/ikigai/tests/conftest.py
!/src/ikigai/tests/test_canonical_scope.py
!/src/ikigai/tests/test_drift_invariants.py
!/src/ikigai/tests/test_gitignore_root_scope.py
!/src/ikigai/tests/test_strategics_loader.py
!/src/ikigai/tests/skills/
!/src/ikigai/tests/contracts/
!/src/ikigai/tests/store/
!/src/ikigai/tests/services/
!/src/ikigai/tests/transport/

